      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# Thinking Space\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "Thinking Space"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 12,
      "raw": "The current project is a Qt 6 Widgets application scaffold. It does not yet\nconsume any workspace SDK package. SDK source projects live in `../../SDK`,\nand installed packages live under `$HOME/.local/SDK`; add a package dependency\nonly when application code actually uses it.\nThe executable links the Core, Gui, and Widgets modules found by CMake.\nIt uses no Qt Quick API, so a fresh configuration does not require a\npreviously cached or indirectly imported `Qt6::Quick` target.\nOn macOS, CMake removes the redundant legacy AGL entry from Qt 6.8's\nOpenGL wrapper so SDKs without AGL can link the app. The Widgets executable keeps\nits normal AppKit and OpenGL dependencies.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 13,
      "end_line": 13,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 14,
      "end_line": 15,
      "raw": "Keep all generated CMake output in `build/`. The CLion Debug profile uses that\nsame directory. Configure and validate from the project directory:\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 16,
      "end_line": 16,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "fenced_code",
      "start_line": 17,
      "end_line": 22,
      "raw": "```sh\ncmake --fresh -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \\\n  -DQt6_DIR=\"/Volumes/Storage/Qt/6.8.3/macos/lib/cmake/Qt6\"\ncmake --build build\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure --no-tests=error\n```\n",
      "language": "sh",
      "code": "cmake --fresh -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \\\n  -DQt6_DIR=\"/Volumes/Storage/Qt/6.8.3/macos/lib/cmake/Qt6\"\ncmake --build build\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure --no-tests=error\n",
      "closed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "b000008",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 23,
      "end_line": 23,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 24,
      "end_line": 25,
      "raw": "No automated application tests are currently registered. The final command\nreports that absence as an error instead of claiming a passing test suite.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000010",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 26,
      "end_line": 26,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000011",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 27,
      "end_line": 27,
      "raw": "## Source layout\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "Source layout"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000012",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 28,
      "end_line": 28,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 29,
      "end_line": 29,
      "raw": "Implementation files and their headers live together under `src/`. Existing feature and platform subdirectories retain their responsibilities. Build configuration, tests, documentation, resources, and maintenance scripts remain at the project root. Configure and build using the repository-local `build/` directory.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000014",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 30,
      "end_line": 30,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
